Client.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them.\n\n- **What triggers a retry:** only `HTTPError` with code 503. Other HTTP errors, timeouts and connection errors are raised right away, as before.\n- **When it gives up:** if the third attempt also gets a 503, that `HTTPError` is passed back to the caller.\n- **New settings:** two constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5` (the first wait, in seconds; each later wait doubles). Existing calls work unchanged.\n\nI checked it against a real local HTTP server rather than a mock:\n- 503, 503, 200 \u2192 returned the data after 3 requests.\n- 503, 503, 503 \u2192 raised the 503 after 3 requests; no fourth request was sent.\n- 500 \u2192 raised immediately after 1 request.\n- 200 \u2192 returned on the first request.\n\nThe server's `Retry-After` header is ignored; the client always uses its own wait times. I didn't add a test file because the repo has no test setup.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34800, "requests_cache_write": 178797, "requests_cost_usd": 0.936801, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1790, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial11", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 80, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:37.512250+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 30.641, "t_checker_s": 2.379, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated",